#: ../../source/templates_zapier.md:16
msgid "1. Visual Theme & Atmosphere"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_zapier.md:18
msgid ""
"Zapier's website radiates warm, approachable professionalism. It rejects "
"the cold monochrome minimalism of developer tools in favor of a cream-"
"tinted canvas (`#fffefb`) that feels like unbleached paper -- the digital"
" equivalent of a well-organized notebook. The near-black (`#201515`) text"
" has a faint reddish-brown warmth, creating an atmosphere more human than"
" mechanical. This is automation designed to feel effortless, not "
"technical."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_zapier.md:20
msgid ""
"The typographic system is a deliberate interplay of two distinct "
"personalities. **Degular Display** -- a geometric, wide-set display face "
"-- handles hero-scale headlines at 56-80px with medium weight (500) and "
"extraordinarily tight line-heights (0.90), creating headlines that "
"compress vertically like stacked blocks. **Inter** serves as the "
"workhorse for everything else, from section headings to body text and "
"navigation, with fallbacks to Helvetica and Arial. **GT Alpina**, an "
"elegant thin-weight serif with aggressive negative letter-spacing (-1.6px"
" to -1.92px), makes occasional appearances for softer editorial moments. "
"This three-font system gives Zapier the ability to shift register -- from"
" bold and punchy (Degular) to clean and functional (Inter) to refined and"
" literary (GT Alpina)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_zapier.md:22
msgid ""
"The brand's signature orange (`#ff4f00`) is unmistakable -- a vivid, "
"saturated red-orange that sits precisely between traffic-cone urgency and"
" sunset warmth. It's used sparingly but decisively: primary CTA buttons, "
"active state underlines, and accent borders. Against the warm cream "
"background, this orange creates a color relationship that feels energetic"
" without being aggressive."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_zapier.md:24
msgid "**Key Characteristics:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_zapier.md:25
msgid ""
"Warm cream canvas (`#fffefb`) instead of pure white -- organic, paper-"
"like warmth"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_zapier.md:26
msgid ""
"Near-black with reddish undertone (`#201515`) -- text that breathes "
"rather than dominates"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_zapier.md:27
msgid ""
"Degular Display for hero headlines at 0.90 line-height -- compressed, "
"impactful, modern"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_zapier.md:28
msgid "Inter as the universal UI font across all functional typography"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_zapier.md:29
msgid ""
"GT Alpina for editorial accents -- thin-weight serif with extreme "
"negative tracking"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_zapier.md:30
msgid ""
"Zapier Orange (`#ff4f00`) as the single accent -- vivid, warm, sparingly "
"applied"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_zapier.md:31
msgid ""
"Warm neutral palette: borders (`#c5c0b1`), muted text (`#939084`), "
"surface tints (`#eceae3`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_zapier.md:32
msgid "8px base spacing system with generous padding on CTAs (20px 24px)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_zapier.md:33
msgid ""
"Border-forward design: `1px solid` borders in warm grays define structure"
" over shadows"
msgstr ""

